        "original_id": "b4955fd3-4cec-5a28-975b-ec678d218f00",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frederic de Hoffmann, Edward Teller\n- Organizations: Los Alamos National Laboratory\n- Products: Hydrogen bomb\n- Roles: Theoretical physicist\n\nFacts:\n- Edward Teller was born in Hungary on January 15, 1908.\n- Edward Teller was a Hungarian-American theoretical physicist.\n- Upon graduating, Frederic de Hoffmann was sent to Los Alamos National Laboratory.\n- At Los Alamos National Laboratory, Frederic de Hoffmann assisted Edward Teller in the development of the hydrogen bomb.\n- Edward Teller was known colloquially as \"the father of the hydrogen bomb,\" although he said he did not care for that title.\n- Edward Teller died on September 9, 2003.",
